  "question": {
    "text": "A square hole of side length $\\ell$ is made at a depth of $\\mathrm{h}$ and a circular hole of radius $\\mathrm{r}$ is made at a depth of $4 \\mathrm{~h}$ from the surface of water in a water tank kept on a horizontal surface. If $\\ell< < h, r< < h$ and the rate of water flow from the holes is the same, then $r$ is equal to<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/scuHmIbukCcuxUc1MsMYHeg-u_09aZI7k7mVrd4DV2c.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "8V7Mi",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\ell}{\\sqrt{2 \\pi}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EhagS",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\ell}{\\sqrt{3 \\pi}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PIFRR",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\ell}{3 \\pi}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "aouEQ",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\ell}{2 \\pi}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As $A_1 v_1=A_2 v_2$ (Principle of continuity) or, $\\ell^2 \\sqrt{2 g h}=\\pi r^2 \\sqrt{2 g \\times 4 h}$\n(Efflux velocity $=\\sqrt{2 \\mathrm{gh}})$\n$\\therefore \\quad r^2=\\frac{\\ell^2}{2 \\pi} \\quad$ or $\\quad r=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\ell^2}{2 \\pi}}=\\frac{\\ell}{\\sqrt{2 \\pi}}$",
    "image": null
  },
